Bugfix: The web interface reports when the server stops assembling an upload

The detached assembly of a large web upload (asynchronous MOVE) now writes
its progress and a timestamp into the job status every ten seconds. The web
interface shows the percentage while "Processing files" and, when the server
has not reported anything for five minutes - for example because a PHP-FPM
reload killed the worker - says so instead of waiting silently. It keeps
checking, removes the notice when the server reports again and gives up with
a clear message after an hour without any report. An error of the assembly
is shown once, with the reason reported by the server and its status code
(507 still cancels the remaining uploads), instead of a second, generic
"status code 202" message.
